Advantages The Singleton pattern offers several benefits when controlled access to a single instance is required:Ensures only one instance exists, preventing inconsistent states.Saves memory and system resources by avoiding multiple object creation.Provides a global access point, making it easy to share the same instance across the application.Limitations Despite its benefits, Singleton can introduce certain design challenges:Can create tight coupling since many classes depend on a global instance.Difficult to unit test due to shared global state.May cause issues in multithreaded environments if not implemented carefully.
